seg-36c9df2abf34 = Signature phase. This phase is performed whether or not the manifest was readable. If the manifest was readable, the <em>named key</em> is <c1/>; if it is not { "64" } lower-case hex digits, failure <c2/> (no named key); otherwise if <c3/> is not the fingerprint of it, failure <c4/> (the key stays usable). If both a <c5/> and a named key exist and differ: failure <c6/>. The <em>check key</em> is <c7/> if one was given, otherwise the named key if there is one; with neither there is no check key (this includes every case where the manifest was not readable and no <c8/> was given). If there is no <c9/>: <c10/>. Else if the file is not exactly { "128" } lower-case hex digits plus one <c11/>: <c12/>. Else if there is a check key that is not a valid Ed25519 public key encoding: <c13/>. Else if there is a check key and the signature does not verify strictly over the bytes of <c14/> (whatever they are): <c15/>. (With no check key the signature is not checked and no failure is raised for that.)

