seg-88359c107bf1 = With <c1/> (one or more PEM certificates, all trusted) <c2/> also checks the authority, offline, the way <c3/> does: the signed attributes' message digest, the signature (RSA PKCS#1 v1.5, RSA-PSS, ECDSA P-256 or P-384), the ESS signing-certificate binding, the signer's critical timeStamping extended key usage, and the chain to a self-issued anchor, every certificate valid at the token's <c4/>. A failure is reported as <c5/> with the first check that failed, and <c6/> is true only when all of it passed. Revocation (CRL or OCSP) is not checked. This verifier agrees with OpenSSL { "3.0.13" } on { "27" } self-generated cases (<c7/>).

