seg-f534ae37f10c = <b>The token sits beside the signed manifest, not inside it.</b> Nothing in the signature or the chain covers it, so a token can be removed, or a different valid token substituted, without the signature failing. <c1/> therefore notes when a pack has none, and <c2/> makes a missing token a failure (<c3/>); a substituted token is caught only if it does not match the manifest. <c4/> refuses to overwrite an existing token unless you pass <c5/>. If a timestamp matters to you, keep the token and the verification result with your own records, and require it.

